WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:01.958
- Growing up so poor

00:00:03.327 --> 00:00:06.307
is why I realized education is important.

00:00:06.307 --> 00:00:09.640
(uplifting piano music)

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.955
My parents came from the old country

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.928
where my father only had
a second grade education,

00:00:25.928 --> 00:00:27.249
my mom had a kindergarten.

00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:29.075
So, it was never really embedded in us

00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:30.921
that education is, especially for a girl,

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:31.964
was that important.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.214
It was more about survival.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.881
My mom was arranged
marriage when she was young

00:00:39.881 --> 00:00:41.955
so already in her head,

00:00:41.955 --> 00:00:44.527
I was gonna be arranged at the age of 16,

00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:45.442
get married.

00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:46.690
And who do I marry?

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.951
Another person who owns
a Chinese restaurant.

00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:51.221
And sure enough at the age of 16,

00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:53.061
I had met my future husband

00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:55.180
who owned a restaurant in Long Island.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.095
I told my mom and dad, no way.

00:00:57.095 --> 00:00:58.469
I want to go to college.

00:00:58.469 --> 00:00:59.800
And it never even dawned on them

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.731
that Heather should go to college.

00:01:01.731 --> 00:01:02.813
And we came to a crossroad

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:04.351
where the lease at the restaurant was up.

00:01:04.351 --> 00:01:06.791
It was at that time when all
my brothers stood up for me

00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:08.785
and said mom and dad,

00:01:08.785 --> 00:01:10.260
I think let's just give up the restaurant.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.833
We all got to do what we got to do

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:14.333
and let Heather go to college.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.922
It was hard because I didn't
have anybody to help me.

00:01:17.922 --> 00:01:19.313
I only applied to three school.

00:01:19.313 --> 00:01:22.398
I only applied to Rutgers, Cornell,

00:01:22.398 --> 00:01:23.557
and like a safety school.

00:01:23.557 --> 00:01:26.200
I wrote my Cornell undergrad in pencil,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.378
my application.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:30.295
I didn't even know to apply in pen.

00:01:31.545 --> 00:01:32.859
I got into Rutgers.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.041
When I got there I didn't
know about financial aid.

00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:37.792
So how did I pay for my
first year of college?

00:01:37.792 --> 00:01:38.986
All my savings since from working

00:01:38.986 --> 00:01:41.107
since was seven years old
in a Chinese restaurant.

00:01:41.107 --> 00:01:43.528
It was then that I met
my college roommates

00:01:43.528 --> 00:01:45.333
and they said, "You paid?

00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:46.626
"You could get financial aid."

00:01:46.626 --> 00:01:49.043
Then people start helping me.

00:01:50.332 --> 00:01:53.446
When I was Taiwan when
I was 17 and visiting

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.674
there was a earthquake.

00:01:54.674 --> 00:01:57.135
I saw the air conditioning
fell on somebody's head.

00:01:57.135 --> 00:02:00.241
I just tilted his head
so that he could breathe

00:02:00.241 --> 00:02:02.534
and I was screaming for help.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:06.534
It was then that I said
I wanted to help people.

00:02:08.826 --> 00:02:12.054
My mom once says, "I wish
Heather would have been a boy,

00:02:12.054 --> 00:02:14.095
"then I could brag about her."

00:02:14.095 --> 00:02:15.293
Yeah.

00:02:15.293 --> 00:02:18.364
Even throughout would I
want to go to grad school,

00:02:18.364 --> 00:02:20.778
my mom was still saying, "Why?

00:02:20.778 --> 00:02:22.247
"Just get married, have kids.

00:02:22.247 --> 00:02:23.850
"That's what you're supposed to be doing."

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.910
Whereas my dad finally dawned on him

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.825
like oh, wow, she actually
could be doing something.

00:02:28.825 --> 00:02:32.242
And gave me $10,000 to go to grad school.

00:02:34.682 --> 00:02:35.762
My brother's daughter,

00:02:35.762 --> 00:02:37.050
I'm really proud of her.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.352
She went to Upenn.

00:02:38.352 --> 00:02:39.343
I give kudos to her,

00:02:39.343 --> 00:02:41.295
she's the first one to graduate
Ivy League in the family.

00:02:41.295 --> 00:02:42.128
Oh but,

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.037
but it's all because of me.

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:44.227
When she was 12,

00:02:44.227 --> 00:02:47.292
I was the one that said
no one ever mentored me

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:48.125
but from day one,

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:49.423
every time it was you're
gonna go to college,

00:02:49.423 --> 00:02:50.256
you're gonna go to college,

00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:51.347
you're going to college.

00:02:51.347 --> 00:02:52.239
If you need any help,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.962
I'll pay for it, yada, yada, yada, yada.

00:02:53.962 --> 00:02:56.647
So that gives them the
confident and support

00:02:56.647 --> 00:02:59.230
that they knew they could have.

00:03:00.652 --> 00:03:04.179
They're quite amazed on how our life,

00:03:04.179 --> 00:03:05.012
even my brother,

00:03:05.012 --> 00:03:06.376
because whatever happened to me

00:03:06.376 --> 00:03:08.860
is also happens to them.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.480
So they really proud.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.966
And of course having my undergrad

00:03:11.966 --> 00:03:14.601
opened the door for me
to go to grad school

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:16.683
which led me to become
the physician assistant

00:03:16.683 --> 00:03:17.771
that I am today.

00:03:17.771 --> 00:03:18.989
If you want to go to college you should,

00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:19.864
you should go to college.

00:03:19.864 --> 00:03:20.697
Go for it!

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.168
(squeaking)

